dm-integrity: don't increment hash_offset twice

jira KERNEL-1700
cve CVE-2026-72099
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.170.1.el8_10
commit-author Mikulas Patocka <mpatocka@redhat.com>
commit edf025f083854f80032b73a1aad69a3c90db236f
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.170.1.el8_10/edf025f0.failed

hash_offset is already incremented in the loop "for (i = 0; i < to_copy;
i++, ts--)". Do not increment it again.

